    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Capture website leads in Fazz and greet new ones on WhatsApp\n\n### How it works\nA visitor fills in an n8n form with their name, WhatsApp number, email and interest. The workflow turns the number into international format, then creates the contact in Fazz or updates the one that already has that number.\n\n- **New contact:** sends your approved welcome template with the visitor's first name and adds a note with their interest.\n- **Existing contact:** adds a note only, so a repeat submission never messages the same person twice.\n- **Welcome not sent** (for example, the template isn't approved for that number): adds a note asking the team to reach out by hand.\n\nThe visitor then sees a thank-you page, or a page asking them to check the number.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node `@fazz-ai/n8n-nodes-fazz` (tested with 0.1.3 on n8n 2.46.6). Until n8n verifies it, it needs self-hosted n8n.\n2. In Fazz, open **Settings › Integrations › Server API**, create a connection and paste its key into a **Fazz API** credential.\n3. In **Send welcome template**, pick your WhatsApp number and a welcome template with one body variable (the first name).\n4. In **Lead settings**, set the lead source name and your default country code.\n5. Activate the workflow and share the form's production URL.\n\n### Customization\nAdd form fields and include them in the notes, or route new leads to a department in the send node's additional fields.",
        "height": 700,
        "width": 500
      },
      "id": "5ae8dd09-b879-40b4-bfea-dddec53d286a",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Collect and check the lead\nCleans the name and email, adds your country code to numbers typed without one, and checks the number's length.",
        "height": 300,
